## Key Observations for Analyst Review

<div style="border-left:4px solid #EF4444;background:#FEF2F2;padding:8px 12px;margin:8px 0;border-radius:4px;">
<span style="background:#FEF2F2;padding:2px 6px;border-radius:4px;"><strong style="color:#EF4444;">PAT Swung to Loss</strong></span><br>
Q1FY26 PAT was <span style="color:#EF4444;font-weight:600">▼ ₹(14.58) crore</span> vs. <strong>₹20.14 crore profit</strong> in Q1FY25 — a sharp YoY deterioration driven by claims outpacing premium growth <doc_source>step1web1</doc_source>.
</div>

<div style="border-left:4px solid #EF4444;background:#FEF2F2;padding:8px 12px;margin:8px 0;border-radius:4px;">
<span style="background:#FEF2F2;padding:2px 6px;border-radius:4px;"><strong style="color:#EF4444;">Combined Ratio Breached Breakeven</strong></span><br>
Combined ratio deteriorated to <span style="color:#EF4444;font-weight:600">▲ 110%</span> (from 101% in Q1FY25), driven by the <strong>claims ratio jumping to 77% from 67%</strong> YoY — Net Incurred Claims rose ~26% YoY to ₹1,215.68 crore, likely reflecting higher claims severity/frequency and/or reserving strengthening <doc_source>step1web1</doc_source>.
</div>

<div style="border-left:4px solid #F59E0B;background:#FFFBEB;padding:8px 12px;margin:8px 0;border-radius:4px;">
<span style="background:#FFFBEB;padding:2px 6px;border-radius:4px;"><strong style="color:#F59E0B;">Growth Deceleration</strong></span><br>
Gross Direct Premium grew only <span style="color:#F59E0B;font-weight:600">~6% YoY</span> in Q1FY26 vs. <strong>~33% YoY</strong> in Q1FY25 — a material slowdown in top-line momentum <doc_source>step1web1</doc_source>.
</div>

<div style="border-left:4px solid #F59E0B;background:#FFFBEB;padding:8px 12px;margin:8px 0;border-radius:4px;">
<span style="background:#FFFBEB;padding:2px 6px;border-radius:4px;"><strong style="color:#F59E0B;">Higher Reinsurance Cession</strong></span><br>
Net Retention Ratio fell to <span style="color:#EF4444;font-weight:600">▼ 77%</span> from <strong>86%</strong> YoY, as reinsurance ceded premium nearly doubled YoY to <strong>₹484.78 crore</strong> from ₹286.99 crore <doc_source>step1web1</doc_source>.
</div>

<div style="border-left:4px solid #22C55E;background:#F0FDF4;padding:8px 12px;margin:8px 0;border-radius:4px;">
<span style="background:#F0FDF4;padding:2px 6px;border-radius:4px;"><strong style="color:#22C55E;">Solvency Remains Comfortable</strong></span><br>
Solvency ratio stood at <span style="color:#22C55E;font-weight:600">▲ 1.66x</span> (above the regulatory minimum of 1.50x), marginally improved from <strong>1.64x</strong> YoY — indicating an adequate capital buffer despite the quarter's underwriting loss <doc_source>step1web1</doc_source>.
</div>

### Data Gaps

Retail-specific GWP/market-share and IFRS-basis figures are **not part of India's IRDAI statutory disclosure framework** and were correctly left blank rather than estimated, per sourcing rules. No separate Q1FY26 investor-presentation deck was available in the source document set; all figures above are statutory IGAAP NL-return values audited under the applicable regulatory framework <doc_source>step1web1</doc_source>.</ans>
